<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.3.4: Writing an Equation to Represent a Relationship</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00098</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.3.4: Writing an Equation to Represent a Relationship</md:title>
    <md:uuid>6ab1bf8d-70e7-44c2-ad78-b2d8a3b2deac</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Clare volunteers at a local library during the summer. Her work includes putting labels on 750 books.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Cool Down Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="d423a733-5c35-4496-b8ac-13fb08612146"><problem><para>
      <para>How many minutes will she need to finish labeling all books if she takes no breaks and labels <emphasis>10 books a minute?
          </emphasis></para>
      <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>75</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is 75.</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section>
<!--Q2 -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Suppose Clare labels the books at a constant speed of \(s\) books per minute. Write an equation that represents
        the relationship between her labeling speed and the number of minutes it would take her to finish labeling.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\( s * m=750 \) or \( m= \frac{750}{s} \), where \(m\) is the number of minutes and \(s\) is
      the speed in books per minute.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End --></section>
</content>
